 "C0": {
  "code": "INELIG",
  "loc": "Title and Abstract, p. 1; Section 1, p. 2",
  "quote": "We also provide tight characterizations of maximally auditable classes of allocation mechanisms",
  "note": "The main object is a theory of auditability for allocation mechanisms (priority-based allocation/school choice, house allocation, object allocation; auctions and reserve rules in the appendix), i.e. matching/fair division rather than a procedure aggregating inputs by voting. Appendix A.3 gives a secondary application characterizing majority voting for binary outcomes, but the paper's main results (Theorems 1-4) concern allocation mechanisms, so the paper is not primarily about a voting procedure."
